% lps-converted-from: umbrella.lps
% This document was written from the LPS program umbrella.lps, which says the same thing in the older syntax. The two run alike, and tools/lps_to_le_test.pl checks that they do. The first line above is what keeps the older file from being read as this document's companion, which would run every rule twice.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 8.

the events are:
    *a thing* forecasts says; known as forecast_says.
    *a thing* goes out.
    it rains.

the actions are:
    *a thing* takes *a second thing*; known as take.
    *a thing* leaves *a second thing*; known as leave.
    *a thing* shelters; known as shelter.

the fluents are:
    the forecast is *a thing*; known as forecast.
    *a thing* is carrying; known as carrying.
    the wet is *a thing*; known as wet.
    the outside is *a thing*; known as outside.
    *a thing* is carrying *a second thing*; known as carrying.

the knowledge base umbrella includes:

initially the forecast is unknown.

when a thing forecasts says
then the forecast that is a second thing becomes the thing.

when a thing goes out
then the outside is the thing.

when a thing takes a second thing
then the thing is carrying the second thing.

when a thing leaves a second thing
then it is not the case that the thing is carrying the second thing.

when it rains
    and the outside is a thing at a time
    and it is not the case that the thing is carrying umbrella at a second time
then the wet is the thing.

if the forecast is rain
    and it is not the case that me is carrying umbrella
then me takes umbrella.

it must not be true that
    the wet is me.


scenario one is:
    rain forecasts says from 2 to 3.
    me goes out from 3 to 4.
    it rains from 5 to 6.
